[b]Keep your surgeon, your steward wife or any other non-fighter out of battle.[/b]

On the [b]Order of Battle[/b] screen, press [b]Keep out of battle[/b] and tick who stays behind.

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]They step out of the line and leave the field unhurt when you press Ready.
[*]They can't be hurt in auto-resolve either.
[*]Your choice is remembered for every later battle, on land and at sea, until you untick them.
[*]The button shows how many are kept out.
[/list]
They still travel with your party, so if the battle is lost they share its fate.

With [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3764210301]Immersive AI[/url], they remember that they were kept back and watched the battle, rather than fought it.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2006]Harmony[/url] (required)
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2102]UIExtenderEx[/url] (required)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] click Mod Manager Download and enable it.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into [i]Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules\[/i], so you get [i]Modules\KeepOutOfBattle\SubModule.xml[/i]. Enable it in the launcher, below Harmony and UIExtenderEx.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer. Works with or without War Sails.
[*]Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.
[*]Also on the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3822341932]Steam Workshop[/url] and on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/keep-out-of-battle/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Same files.
[/list]

Bugs or a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/keep-out-of-battle/issues]GitHub[/url]. How it works in detail: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/keep-out-of-battle/blob/main/docs/TECHNICAL.md]docs/TECHNICAL.md[/url].

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

